# Files kept in git but deliberately left out of the Comfy Registry archive.
# Syntax matches .gitignore. See https://docs.comfy.org/registry/publishing
#
# Everything here is development or presentation material. None of it is needed
# to run a single node, and all of it is still on GitHub for anyone who wants it.

# Test suite. The registry docs name tests as the example of what to exclude,
# and test_adversarial_repairs.py is full of attack-shaped vocabulary that a
# security scan has no way to tell apart from the real thing.
tests/

# CI configuration. It references a publishing token by name and does nothing
# at runtime.
.github/

# Repository housekeeping.
.gitignore

# Promotional image, 8.3 MB. It is what the README shows on GitHub; nobody
# needs it sitting in their custom_nodes folder.
